Subject: Fix case-sensitive include of Error.h in NWfill.c

Upstream NWfill.c includes "error.h" (lowercase) while the header file
is Error.h (uppercase E). It resolves on case-insensitive filesystems
(macOS, where upstream is developed) but is a hard error on
case-sensitive ones (Linux, OHOS):
    NWfill.c:39:10: fatal error: 'error.h' file not found

--- a/NWfill.c
+++ b/NWfill.c
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
 #include <float.h>
 #include <time.h>
 #include "distfit.h"
-#include "error.h"
+#include "Error.h"
 #include "DLTutils.h"
 #include "pdbMalloc.h"
 #include "pdbIO.h"
